Principle Where How Single responsibility <code>RoleChangeView</code>, <code>RoleChangeSerializer</code>, <code>AuthService.change_role</code> The view speaks HTTP, the serializer validates the one input, and the service owns the rule, the update and the log. Each changes for one reason. On mobile, <code>_changeableRoleTitle</code> decides and <code>build</code> lays out. Open/closed The new endpoint and <code>UserRoleChangeLog</code> Role changes arrive as an addition. <code>register_with_google</code>, <code>GoogleRegistrationView</code> and <code>IsRegistrationRole</code> are untouched, and the existing <code>_session_response</code> is reused, not edited. Liskov substitution Every <code>AuthRepository</code> implementation <code>AuthRepositoryImpl</code>, the offline preview session and the test doubles all gained <code>changeRole</code> with the same contract: a session on success, a failure on refusal. Any of them can stand in for the real one, which is what lets the page and notifier tests run without a server. Interface segregation <code>RoleChangeSerializer</code>, <code>AuthRemoteDataSources.changeRole(String role)</code> A client changing a role sends one field. It doesn't go through the registration serializer, which also needs a <code>registration_token</code>. Dependency inversion <code>AuthenticationNotifier</code> → <code>LoginWithGoogleUseCase</code> → <code>AuthRepository</code> The notifier depends on the use case, and the use case on the repository interface. Tests inject mocktail mocks at each level. lib/features/authentication/presentation/providers/authentication_provider.dart<pre><code>/// Switches a registering account to [role]. Returns null once the session
/// for the new role is in place, or the server's reason when the change is
/// refused, in which case the current session is left as it was.
Future&lt;String?&gt; changeRole(GoogleRegistrationRole role) async {
  final result = await _loginWithGoogleUseCase.changeRole(role);
  return result.fold(
    (failure) =&gt; failure.displayMessage,
    (entity) {
      _emitAuthenticated(entity);
      return null;
    },
  );
}
</code></pre>

Behaviour Red Green The red failed on The data layer PATCHes <code>onboarding/role</code>, stores the new session, and keeps the old one on a 409 <code>8ef4514</code> <code>f8214e3</code> Compile error: <code>changeRole</code> isn't defined The notifier switches to the new session, or returns the server's reason and keeps the old one <code>79f95a9</code> <code>778cad5</code> Compile error: <code>changeRole</code> isn't defined The role page serves a signed-in account: its identity without "Ganti akun", its role preselected, the change made, the draft dropped, a refusal shown; an account past the profile step still goes to login <code>a0b8fd0</code> <code>9517dbd</code> <code>Found 0 widgets with text "Daftar Akun"</code>: the page sent every account without a registration token to login Lengkapi Profil names the role and links to change it; the link is hidden once a bank sampah exists or in invite mode; the form redraws for a new role <code>9e83120</code> <code>a1b49bd</code> No label. I also ran the redraw test with the label assertion removed, and it still failed: the screen kept the pengurus stepper. So that test proves the redraw, not just the label <p>Refactor after green:</p> <ul> <li><code>2589b0b</code> turned the role page's nested-ternary <code>onPressed</code> into <code>_submit</code>.</li> <li><code>87f2f0d</code> moved the role-note rule out of <code>build</code>, after SonarCloud's S3776 finding.</li> </ul> <p>The same tests passed before and after each.</p> <p>Coverage tests, added after the behaviour was in place:</p> <ul> <li><code>d3d3dba</code>: the preview session's <code>changeRole</code>.</li> <li><code>c578399</code>: a malformed 2xx body becomes a <code>Left</code> instead of crashing.</li> <li><code>b2344b5</code>: <code>getMe</code> and <code>saveToken</code>.</li> </ul> <p>The mock with captured arguments, from the data-layer test:</p> test/features/authentication/data/auth_repository_impl_test.dart<pre><code>test('stores the session issued for the new role', () async {
  when(() =&gt; remote.changeRole('nasabah')).thenAnswer(
    (_) async =&gt; &lt;String, dynamic&gt;{
      'access_token': 'access-new',
      'refresh_token': 'refresh-new',
      'user': {
        'id': 'user-1',
        'name': 'Ayu',
        'email': 'ayu@example.com',
        'role': 'nasabah',
      },
      'next_step': 'complete_profile',
    },
  );
  when(() =&gt; local.saveToken(any())).thenAnswer((_) async {});

  final result = await repo.changeRole(GoogleRegistrationRole.nasabah);

  final auth = result.getOrElse(() =&gt; throw 'expected a session');
  expect(auth.role, 'nasabah');
  expect(auth.nextStep, 'complete_profile');
  final saved = verify(() =&gt; local.saveToken(captureAny())).captured.single
      as SaveTokenRequest;
  expect(saved.accessToken, 'access-new');
  expect(saved.refreshToken, 'refresh-new');
});
</code></pre>

Rule Where Fix <code>python:S9073</code> Split this composite assertion <code>apps/waste_catalog/test_harga_versi.py</code>, #79 <code>fe5db58</code>. <code>assert a is not None and b is not None</code> became two asserts, so a failure names the missing value. They stay plain <code>assert</code>s, because mypy narrows types on those and not on <code>assertIsNotNone</code>. <code>dart:S3358</code> Extract this nested ternary operation <code>tambah_jenis_sampah_bottom_sheet.dart:456</code>, #62 Test-first: <code>2fca502</code> <code>[RED]</code> → <code>47a2160</code> <code>[GREEN]</code> → <code>2ce3dab</code> <code>[REFACTOR]</code>. The success message choice moved into <code>pesanSimpanJenis</code>, a pure function with its own tests; the sheet just passes what happened. lib/features/harga/presentation/widgets/pesan_simpan_jenis.dart<pre><code>String pesanSimpanJenis({
  required bool isEditMode,
  required bool hargaBerubah,
  DateTime? berlakuMulai,
}) {
  if (!isEditMode) return 'Jenis sampah baru berhasil ditambahkan.';
  if (hargaBerubah &amp;&amp; berlakuMulai != null) {
    return 'Harga baru berlaku mulai ${formatTanggalId(berlakuMulai)}.';
  }
  return 'Jenis sampah berhasil diperbarui.';
}
</code></pre>
